A) The information provided to the data subject at the time of data collection shall include at least the following information:
a.1) Controller Details: the identity of and contact details of the Controller;
a.3) DPO Contact: the contact details of the data protection officer (or contact mechanism);
a.4) Purpose: the purposes of processing;
a.5) Legal Basis: the legal basis for the processing;
a.6) Legitimate Interests: if applicable, the legitimate interests pursued by the Controller or by a third-party;
a.7) Recipients: the recipients or categories of recipients of the personal data;
a.8) Cross border transfer: if personal data are likely to be transferred to any third country or to an international organization, the list of non-European countries where the data are transferred;
a.9) Cross border transfer: if personal data are likely to be transferred to any third country or to an international organization, whether a valid adequacy decision applies to the data transfer;
a.10) Cross border transfer: if personal data are likely to be transferred to any third country or to an international organization, information on the safeguards measures adopted by the Controller to assess and minimize the risks for the data subjects and their rights when processed in third-countries;
a.11) Automated decision-making: if automated decision-making and/or profiling is performed, meaningful information about the logic involved in the processing activities;
a.12) Automated decision-making: if automated decision-making and/or profiling is performed, the significance of the processing activities;
a.13) Automated decision-making: if automated decision-making and/or profiling is performed, the envisaged consequences of the processing activities;
a.14) Period of Retention: the retention period or the criteria for determining the retention period;
a.15) Data Subject Rights: information on the data subject's rights to:
- access to personal data,
- rectification of personal data, 
- erasure of personal data, 
- restriction of data processing;
- objection to data processing;
- to data portability;
- withdraw consent at any time (if processing is based on consent) 
- lodge a complaint with the Supervisory Authority; *(AND)*

a.16) Nature of Requirement: whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data.

A) The Applicant shall have a procedure or mechanism in place for data portability that: 
